---
/**
 * How a public request reaches your machine. Theme-aware via CSS vars and
 * fluid via viewBox — no fixed pixel width.
 */
---

<figure class="my-7">
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 720 300"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="arch-title arch-desc"
    class="w-full rounded-xl border border-border/80 bg-card p-3"
  >
    <title id="arch-title">How a request reaches your local app</title>
    <desc id="arch-desc">
      A visitor's browser reaches the OctoPort service, which looks up which client owns that
      address and forwards the request down the connection your client already opened. The client
      passes it to your local app and the response travels back the same way.
    </desc>

    <defs>
      <marker id="arch-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto">
        <path d="M0 0 10 5 0 10z" fill="var(--muted-foreground)"></path>
      </marker>
    </defs>

    <g
      font-family="var(--font-sans)"
      font-size="12"
      fill="var(--foreground)"
      stroke-linecap="round"
    >
      <!-- visitor -->
      <rect x="12" y="112" width="112" height="52" rx="10" fill="var(--muted)" stroke="var(--border)"></rect>
      <text x="68" y="134" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">Visitor</text>
      <text x="68" y="150" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted-foreground)" font-size="10.5">browser / curl</text>

      <!-- control plane -->
      <rect
        x="196"
        y="40"
        width="234"
        height="200"
        rx="14"
        fill="none"
        stroke="var(--primary)"
        stroke-dasharray="4 4"
        opacity="0.65"></rect>
      <text x="313" y="62" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="600" fill="var(--primary)">
        OCTOPORT SERVICE (we run this)
      </text>

      <rect x="214" y="78" width="198" height="46" rx="9" fill="var(--muted)" stroke="var(--border)"></rect>
      <text x="313" y="97" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">Receives the request</text>
      <text x="313" y="112" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted-foreground)" font-size="10.5">
        https://k7xq2p9m.itanishq.space
      </text>

      <rect x="214" y="136" width="198" height="42" rx="9" fill="var(--muted)" stroke="var(--border)"></rect>
      <text x="313" y="153" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">Finds your tunnel</text>
      <text x="313" y="168" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted-foreground)" font-size="10.5">
        address → your client
      </text>

      <rect x="214" y="190" width="198" height="36" rx="9" fill="var(--muted)" stroke="var(--border)"></rect>
      <text x="313" y="212" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">Sends it down your connection</text>

      <!-- agent -->
      <rect x="502" y="88" width="120" height="52" rx="10" fill="var(--muted)" stroke="var(--border)"></rect>
      <text x="562" y="110" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">OctoPort client</text>
      <text x="562" y="126" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted-foreground)" font-size="10.5">CLI or desktop app</text>

      <!-- local app -->
      <rect x="502" y="186" width="120" height="52" rx="10" fill="var(--muted)" stroke="var(--border)"></rect>
      <text x="562" y="208" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">Your app</text>
      <text x="562" y="224" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted-foreground)" font-size="10.5">localhost:3000</text>

      <!-- your machine boundary -->
      <rect
        x="486"
        y="66"
        width="152"
        height="188"
        rx="14"
        fill="none"
        stroke="var(--border)"
        stroke-dasharray="4 4"></rect>
      <text x="562" y="270" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--muted-foreground)">
        your machine · no inbound ports
      </text>

      <!-- arrows -->
      <g stroke="var(--muted-foreground)" stroke-width="1.4" fill="none" marker-end="url(#arch-arrow)">
        <path d="M126 132 H208"></path>
        <path d="M414 106 H496"></path>
        <path d="M562 142 V182"></path>
      </g>

      <g font-size="10" fill="var(--muted-foreground)" text-anchor="middle">
        <text x="167" y="124">HTTPS</text>
        <text x="455" y="98">one connection</text>
        <text x="455" y="112" font-size="9">(opened by your client)</text>
        <text x="588" y="166" text-anchor="start">TCP</text>
      </g>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
    Your client opens the only connection that crosses your network boundary, and it opens it
    outward — so there is nothing to configure and nothing on your machine listening for
    strangers.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
